Z||000004||Standard||02-17-2000||02:02 AM||||wow, that really bites the big one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I hope you get it back!  about a 2 months ago our neighbors car was broken in to, and a few days ago another car was broken in to a few houses away.  police say there's been a few cars broken into in this area.. both my Fiero's are outside, and I'm real nervous with both of them sittin' out there...||||reg||9
Z||000005||Greg Piet||02-17-2000||03:07 AM||||I realize this is after the fact, and I feel for your loss.  I put todays car thiefs in the class of a horse thief from years past.  If I had it my way there would still be hangings for horse/car thiefs.  "You just don't mess with a mans car dammit!"<P>In my paranoid state, with all my cars I have a number of extra kill switches, ranging from fuel pump switch, distributor switch, and the always beefy battery kill switch.  Sure they might bash the heck out of your column to make the key unnecessary, but if they dont know where to look for these other well hidden simple switches they wont get anywhere.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||02-17-2000||04:07 AM||||geez.. that really sucks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I'm concerned about that happening to me, so I've been reading up on ultrasonics.. no matter how badly a person might want my car.. I doubt anyone could stand several 130db sirens, strobe lights, etc.. too bad tesla coils would be illegal in a security system..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>What about a keypad, in the car? type in a code and then the key will work.. do any security systems use something like that?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||02-17-2000||04:53 AM||||DarkLord, that's the system I have in my car. You need to type in a code - otherwise the car just won't start<P>FieroSTETZ, that really, really sucks. Let's hope it's just a joyrider and they'll find your car in tact one of these days.||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChadMan||02-17-2000||09:14 AM||||Aw, STETZ, that's terrible.  Like Cliff, I hope you get your baby back (baby-back baby-back baby-back...)<P>Car thieves are scum, but I think I hate vandals even more.  At least a thief screws you over for his own personal gain.  A vandal just wants to ruin what you've worked hard to earn.||||reg||9
Z||000009||deceler8||02-17-2000||09:18 AM||||How about a pound of plastique and a cellular detonator ? Car shows up missing and you phone in the "mother of all solutions" to auto theft...<P>And all you have to tell the cops is that you didn't have time to fix that oil leak...<P>Really amazing that cars our age are still theft-prone. Of course, GM cars of the frameless-door era were the most stolen in their day and apparently still are now. ||||reg||10
Z||000010||FieroSTETZ||02-17-2000||11:04 AM||||well, I am 17 and couldn't afford a lot in the way of insurance. I was paying for what i had now by doing lots of odd jobs and helping people out with their computers. I didn't have a lot of money so all I had was liability. Now I am a technician at CompUSA and I was hoping to bump my insurance up to full as soon as I started getting paid. I have a few friends with the local police, so i called in a favor and so i have a few cops "keeping an eye out" for a gold fiero with a chrome pegasus hood ornament.||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfiero||02-17-2000||11:49 AM||||That truly does stink.  I had an '88 GT stolen about 6 years ago.  A friend of mine and myself went to a Denver Nuggets basketball game (when they were a good team!) and it was stolen right from the arena lot.  I had just gotten new balljoints installed, but didn't have it aligned, and the MAP sensor kept unplugging itself.  I think the combination of poor handling and rough driving caused them to abandon it sooner because it was found about 8 hours later (less than 1 mile from the arena.).<P>The odds are good that they are just joy riders.....as much as I love Fieros there just isn't a black market for them.  Why steal a 12-15 year old car when a new Civic will bring more $$$ from a chop shop?  Hopefully they just leave it somewhere and don't purposely destroy it.<P>Let us know how things progress.    ||||reg||8
Z||000012||fiero56||02-17-2000||11:58 AM||||Being on several fiero lists, I've probably heard of a dozen people having their Fiero stolen. From what I've noticed all of them have found the Fiero within 3-4 days, abandoned in a parking lot. Some with very little damage, some torn up. We don't have very many parts worth any money, just a joy ride kind of stealing. Too bad about yours, I hope you find it in good condition.<P>Cliff, I would love to see a picture of your keypad. Did you make it yourself, or is there a kit you bought?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||DRH||02-17-2000||03:43 PM||||FieroSTETZ, That is a real pi$$er. I hope it turns up unharmed.<P>Along the lines of a kill switch... if your E-brake works... use it... I'm guessing the average joyrider couldn't figure out how to release it!!!||||reg||9
